Description: Add an iwlmvm "country" parameter that fixes the regulatory country
 Devices with location-aware regulatory (LAR) get their country from the BIOS
 (ACPI) or, failing that, guess it from nearby beacons. Device-tree platforms
 such as Jetson have no BIOS country, so the firmware starts on the world
 domain, where every 6 GHz channel is disabled, and a 6 GHz-only network
 can't be found until the firmware's guess comes in. Whenever the station is
 not associated the firmware guesses again, every few seconds, and one nearby
 device advertising the wrong country is enough to move it.
 .
 With iwlmvm country=XX (ISO 3166 alpha-2), the driver sets that country when
 the firmware starts, in the same way as the SET_COUNTRY vendor command (MCC
 API source), and firmware restarts replay it through the existing
 iwl_mvm_init_fw_regd() path. The firmware applies its own guesses before it
 reports them (MCC_CHUB_UPDATE), so each report is answered by setting the
 fixed country again; only ignoring them left the firmware on its guess, with
 no 6 GHz, until it restarted, while the host still showed the fixed country.
 Without the parameter nothing changes.
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-09-30
